1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,262
The Invention of Paper.

2
00:00:02,212 --> 00:00:15,200
Paper was invented in China around 105 CE by Cai Lun, a Han court official who processed tree bark, hemp, rags, and fishing nets by soaking, beating into pulp, and pressing into thin sheets.

3
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:26,537
The technology spread to Korea and Japan in the 7th century, reached the Islamic world after the Battle of Talas in 751 CE, and arrived in Europe in the 12th century.

4
00:00:26,537 --> 00:00:30,687
Gutenberg's printing press dramatically increased paper demand.

5
00:00:30,687 --> 00:00:40,050
Modern global paper production exceeds 400 million metric tons annually, though digital media is reducing demand for printing and writing grades.

6
00:00:40,050 --> 00:00:47,350
Paper remains essential for packaging, hygiene products, and specialized industrial applications around the world.

